minkipc for Debian
==================

MinkIPC is Qualcomm's lightweight capability-based inter-process
communication (IPC) framework built on the MINK ('Mink is Not a Kernel')
security paradigm.  It enables secure, synchronous message passing across
different security domains — such as Linux user space to the Qualcomm
Trusted Execution Environment (QTEE) — using unforgeable object references
and transport mechanisms including SMC calls, sockets, and TEE IOCTLs.

Packages
--------

libminkadaptor0
  Shared library that implements the userspace MinkIPC interface.  It
  provides the low-level Object_invoke transport layer used to communicate
  with QTEE via the QCOM-TEE driver registered with the Linux TEE subsystem.

libminkteec1
  Shared library that implements the GlobalPlatform TEE Client API (GP TEE
  Client API v1.0) on top of MinkIPC. Applications that use the standard
  GP TEEC interface can use this library to communicate with Trusted
  Applications running in QTEE.

libminkipc-dev
  Development headers and linker symlinks for libminkadaptor0 and
  libminkteec1. Required when building software that links against either
  of those libraries.

minkipc-qteesupplicant
  The qteesupplicant and sfsconfig daemons, their systemd service units,
  and the udev rules needed for user-space access to QTEE.  The supplicant
  handles requests from the TEE that require Linux-side resources (e.g.
  file-system access, RPMB storage).

minkipc-tools
  Userspace utilities for interacting with MinkIPC services.  Currently
  includes rpmb_client for provisioning the Replay Protected Memory Block.

minkipc-tests
  Test binaries for validating MinkIPC functionality, including
  smcinvoke_client (SMC invocation testing) and gp_test_client
  (GlobalPlatform TEE API conformance testing). Intended for development
  and integration verification; not required on production systems.

Known Limitations
-----------------

PKCS#11 libraries, client utilities, and the corresponding Trusted
Applications (TAs) are not packaged as part of this source package. 
